{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":5533,"output":338,"cacheRead":10133,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":16004,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The bug: In HomeScreen, `CategoriesSidebar` is called without `onOpenRestore`, so the default `onOpenRestore = {}` no-op applies. Hence clicking Restore in sidebar has no effect. Fix: pass `onOpenRestore` in HomeScreen so it navigates to Restore route.\n\nSecond part: The two `Restore` buttons flanking the balance box on the Home screen should instead open transaction history for the month (same as clicking the balance box), and they should use the hamburger menu icon (3 horizontal lines) instead of the Restore icon.\n\nSo HomeScreen: replace those IconButtons with hamburger icon (Icons.Outlined.Menu) and onClick = onOpenTransactionHistory.\n\nNow tests. Tests in app/src/test are unit tests. There's `TransactionHistoryScreenTest.kt` in app/src/test — a unit test for a Compose screen? Let me look at existing test files to see how UI-related tests are done, e.g. TransactionHistoryScreenTest.kt and the androidTest BudgetAppSmokeTest.kt.\n"}}
