{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":879,"output":774,"cacheRead":24138,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":25791,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now, let's decide the implementation.\n\nFix plan:\n\n1. `CategoriesSidebar`: make `onOpenRestore: () -> Unit` a required parameter (remove `= {}` default) so a missing wiring is a compile error.\n\n2. `HomeScreen`: pass `onOpenRestore` to `CategoriesSidebar` (closing sidebar then navigating). Note the sidebar animation exit — calling onClose then navigate is fine (navigation replaces the screen). Actually navigating away unmounts HomeScreen immediately; sidebar animation exit won't matter.\n\n3. HomeScreen balance-row: left and right IconButtons → `Icons.Outlined.Menu` (hamburger) icons, `onClick = onOpenTransactionHistory`, contentDescription \"Open transaction history\", plus testTags `balance_history_left`, `balance_history_right`.\n\n4. Keep `onOpenRestore` parameter on HomeScreen signature? HomeScreen now uses it for the sidebar. Yes, it's used.\n\n5. `onOpenTransactionHistorySwipe` — check whether it's used anywhere. In HomeScreen it's a parameter; grep shows... In HomeScreen body I didn't see usage. Unused parameter. Not my concern (out of scope), though could leave.\n\nTests:\n- Add an androidTest UI test (Compose) verifying: sidebar Restore click navigates to Restore screen; balance-side buttons open transaction history and show hamburger icon not Restore icon. This is the right test kind for UI behaviour, and repo has precedent (BudgetAppSmokeTest with createAndroidComposeRule<MainActivity>). It won't be run by harness verify (needs emulator), but AGENTS.md says connectedDebugAndroidTest needs an emulator and is kept out of verify_commands.\n\nHmm, but harness requires test changes under test globs — androidTest counts. But \"Run the tests yourself and iterate until they are green\" — I can't run androidTest without an emulator. Let me check if an emulator/device is available: `adb devices`.\n\n- Also add a JVM unit test that guards the wiring in a way runnable by testDebugUnitTest. Options: a source-inspection test similar to GradleDeprecationWarningsTest precedent: e.g. `HomeScreenWiringTest` asserting:\n  - `HomeScreen.kt` passes `onOpenRestore =` to `CategoriesSidebar(` call.\n  - `HomeScreen.kt` no longer uses `Icons.Outlined.Restore` and uses `Icons.Outlined.Menu` for the balance side buttons.\n  - `CategoriesSidebar.kt` has no default no-op `onOpenRestore = {}` parameter.\n\nThat's a bit fragile but it is genuinely a guard test and there's precedent in this repo. Combined with a compile-time enforcement (required parameter), it's reasonable.\n\nBetter: make the check robust by parsing? Keep simple string checks with clear messages.\n\nLet's also check MainActivity to see how MainActivity sets content — for androidTest to work on the home screen.\n\nAlso consider whether Restore in the sidebar should also close the sidebar. And check RestoreScreen for onBack.\n\nLet me check MainActivity and RestoreScreen.\n"}}
