{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":56,"output":975,"cacheRead":37717,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":38748,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now check exact source formatting for the assertions, e.g. balance box clickable:\n\n```\n                    .clickable(\n                        interactionSource = remember { MutableInteractionSource() },\n                        indication = null,\n                    ) {\n                        onOpenTransactionHistory()\n                    },\n```\nYes that matches \"{\\n                        onOpenTransactionHistory()\\n                    },\".\n\nAlso the CategoriesSidebar call substringBefore(\"\\n            )\") — the call in HomeScreen:\n```\n            CategoriesSidebar(\n                categories = allCategories,\n                ...\n                onOpenRestore = {\n                    sidebarOpen = false\n                    onOpenRestore()\n                },\n            )\n```\n`substringAfter(\"CategoriesSidebar(\")` — careful: the import line `import com.lorenzo.monefyme.ui.component.CategoriesSidebar` doesn't include \"CategoriesSidebar(\" — good, no paren. substringBefore(\"\\n            )\") → the closing is at 12 spaces indent: `            )`. Yes since inside `AnimatedVisibility(` block at 8... let me verify indentation: AnimatedVisibility( ... ) { then `            CategoriesSidebar(` at 12 spaces, and closing `            )` at 12. Good.\n\nWait — but there's a nested `onOpenRestore = {` block closing `                },` — fine, and the first occurrence of \"\\n            )\" after \"CategoriesSidebar(\" — is there any line at exactly 12 spaces `)` earlier? Inside the call, params are at 16 spaces. So fine.\n\nNow write the androidTest.\n"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":56,"output":975,"cacheRead":37717,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":38748,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_af81b06d5e36488cbad92511","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"package com.lorenzo.monefyme.ui\n\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.assertCountEquals\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.assertIsDisplayed\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.assert\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.hasClickAction\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.junit4.createAndroidComposeRule\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.onAllNodesWithContentDescription\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.onNodeWithTag\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.onNodeWithText\nimport androidx.compose.ui.test.performClick\nimport com.lorenzo.monefyme.MainActivity\nimport org.junit.Rule\nimport org.junit.Test\n\n/**\n * End-to-end coverage for the Home screen \"Restore\" entry points.\n *\n * - The sidebar \"Restore\" row must open the Restore screen (it used to be a silent no-op because\n *   HomeScreen never passed the sidebar's onOpenRestore callback).\n * - The two buttons next to the balance box must open the month's transaction history (like the\n *   balance box itself) and must carry the hamburger icon, not the Restore icon.\n */\nclass HomeRestoreNavigationTest {\n\n    @get:Rule\n    val composeTestRule = createAndroidComposeRule<MainActivity>()\n\n    @Test\n    fun sidebarRestoreRowOpensRestoreScreen() {\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithText(\"Monefy\").assertIsDisplayed()\n\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithContentDescription(\"More\").performClick()\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithTag(\"sidebar_restore\").assertIsDisplayed().assert(hasClickAction())\n\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithTag(\"sidebar_restore\").performClick()\n\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithText(\"Manual CSV restore\").assertIsDisplayed()\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun balanceBoxLeftButtonOpensTransactionHistory() {\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithTag(\"balance_history_left\")\n            .assert(hasClickAction())\n            .performClick()\n\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithText(\"Transactions\").assertIsDisplayed()\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun balanceBoxRightButtonOpensTransactionHistory() {\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithTag(\"balance_history_right\")\n            .assert(hasClickAction())\n            .performClick()\n\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithText(\"Transactions\").assertIsDisplayed()\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun balanceBoxSideButtonsUseHamburgerIconsAndNotRestoreIcons() {\n        composeTestRule.onAllNodesWithContentDescription(\"Open transaction history\")\n            .assertCountEquals(2)\n        // The Restore entry point now lives only in the sidebar, so the closed Home screen must\n        // not expose a Restore button any more.\n        composeTestRule.onNodeWithContentDescription(\"Open restore\").assertDoesNotExist()\n    }\n}\n","path":"C:\\p\\monefyme\\app\\src\\androidTest\\java\\com\\lorenzo\\monefyme\\ui\\HomeRestoreNavigationTest.kt"}}}}
