`sidebarMenuItems(onOpenCategories, onOpenRestore)` as a pure function that MenuBody renders from a list. Then a JVM unit test can call that function and assert the Restore entry invokes onOpenRestore. That's a real behavioural test of the sidebar menu wiring and reasonably clean, not over-abstraction — modest refactor of MenuBody to iterate over entries. But it doesn't test that HomeScreen wires onOpenRestore.\n\nCombine: keep it simpler — source-based guard tests plus the real UI test in androidTest. I think I'll do both:\n1. JVM guard test: source-level wiring assertions (documented rationale), runnable by harness verify.\n2. androidTest UI test: real behaviour.\n\nLet me also double-check the \"Restore\" row in MenuBody — clicking the row calls onOpenRestore. Fine.\n\nAdditionally, should the sidebar's Restore item still show the Restore icon? Yes, task only says Home's balance-side buttons shouldn't have the Restore icon.\n\nNow write the code.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me make the changes. First, `HomeScreen.kt`:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f80f36021ad54a9ca21bf712","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"C:\\p\\monefyme\\app\\src\\main\\java\\com\\lorenzo\\monefyme\\ui\\screen\\HomeScreen.kt","edits":[{"oldText":"import androidx.compose.material.icons.outlined.ChevronRight\nimport androidx.compose.material.icons.outlined.MoreVert\nimport androidx.compose.material.icons.outlined.Restore\n","newText":"import androidx.compose.material.icons.outlined.ChevronRight\nimport androidx.compose.material.icons.outlined.Menu\nimport androidx.compose.material.icons.outlined.MoreVert\n"},{"oldText":"            horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.SpaceBetween,\n        ) {\n            IconButton(\n                onClick = onOpenRestore,\n                modifier = Modifier.size(40.dp),\n            ) {\n                Icon(\n                    imageVector = Icons.Outlined.Restore,\n                    contentDescription = 